+#   - `EPILOGUE_MODE == 0`: standard contiguous `[M, N]` output.
+#   - `EPILOGUE_MODE == 1`: de-interleaves 64/128-col interleaved `[Gate, Up]` back into
+#     contiguous `[Gate (N/2), Up (N/2)]` halves when unfused linear output is requested.
+#   - `EPILOGUE_MODE == 2`: fused `[Gate, Up] -> SwiGLU -> Hadamard-64` writing `[M, N/2]`;
+#     when `BLOCK_N == 128` and `BLOCK_M >= 32`, fuses both 128-col halves into a single
+#     wide `[BLOCK_M, 256]` INT8 SME `tl.dot` (`BN_FULL = 256`) and splits `(g, u)` in VGPRs.
