+"""Composable Pure-Triton W8A8 Matrix Core GEMM for MetaX C500 (`xcore1000`),
+registered with `flag_gems.utils.quant_config`.
+
+Architectural Highlights on MetaX C500 (`104` Active CUs, `warp_size=64`, `580` TOPS INT8):
+1. **Law of Direct-Operand DMA (`global_load_lds_dwordx4`)**:
+   On `xcore1000`, hardware async HBM -> LDS DMA (`900-1,523 GB/s`, bypassing VGPRs) triggers
+   ONLY when `tl.load` uses a uniform SGPR base descriptor (`tl.multiple_of` + `tl.max_contiguous`)
+   and feeds a homogeneous `INT8 x INT8 -> INT32` `tl.dot` (`16x16x32i8`) with ZERO intervening
+   VALU casts (`i8 -> bf16`). Per-token `SA` and per-channel `SB` FP32 dequantization is applied
+   strictly once in the epilogue after the full K-loop completes.
+2. **Single-Launch 2-Region Composite N-Tiling (`_unified_w8a8_nt_kernel`)**:
+   Partitions `N` into primary `R0` tiles (`SUB_N0_A + SUB_N1_A`) and secondary `R1` tiles
+   (`SUB_N0_B + SUB_N1_B`) so total CTAs align to exact multiples of `104` CUs with `LDS <= 32 KiB`
+   (`2 CTAs/CU` co-residency under `pipeline="basic"`).
+3. **1-Kernel Atomic Split-K vs. 2-Stage Workspace Split-K**:
+   Small-M Decode chooses between L2-resident single-launch `acq_rel`/`release` spin-free atomic
+   reduction (`_unified_w8a8_1k_splitk_kernel`) and 2-stage BF16 partial reduction supporting
+   multi-group activation scales (`_unified_w8a8_2s_splitk_kernel` + `_w8a8_reduce_splitk_kernel`).
+"""
